course: dictionary
lesson: 3746
title: Flu: an illness caused by a virus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Flu is short for influenza. It is an illness caused by a virus, which is a tiny germ too small to see. «Flu comes on suddenly with high fever, aching muscles, headache, shivers and great tiredness.» These clues tell you what flu feels like.
explain: Flu is not the same as a cold, although both are caused by viruses. Flu is worse, and it comes on suddenly. «Colds and flu are caused by viruses, tiny germs that travel in the drops we sneeze and cough out and in our spit.»
explain: Viruses spread when we cough, sneeze or touch things with dirty hands. That is why we cover a cough with a tissue or our elbow and wash our hands. The children's flu vaccine is a nasal spray, and it changes every year because flu viruses change.
fact: Flu is an illness caused by a virus.
fact: Flu usually gives you a high temperature, aches, a cough, a sore throat and great tiredness.
fact: Flu is worse than a common cold.
fact: Antibiotics kill bacteria but do nothing to viruses, so they do not help flu.
fact: A flu jab or flu shot helps protect you from flu, and many people have one every year.
exercise: «Flu comes on suddenly with high fever, aching muscles, headache, shivers and great tiredness.» What causes flu? | Walking in the rain | Too much sugar | A cold wind | *A virus, a tiny germ
exercise: Which of these is a sign of flu? | Wanting to run a marathon | *Great tiredness | A sudden urge to swim | Feeling wide awake and full of energy
exercise: «Colds and flu are caused by viruses, tiny germs that travel in the drops we sneeze and cough out.» How do flu germs usually spread? | Through the sunshine | Through eating apples | By looking at the moon | *In the drops we cough and sneeze out, and on dirty hands
test: Why do antibiotics not help flu? | Because flu is too big to see | Because antibiotics make flu worse every time | Because flu only happens in summer | *Because antibiotics do nothing to viruses
test: Why does the flu vaccine change every year? | Because the needle gets blunt | Because the nurses change | Because it tastes better each year | *Because flu viruses change
exam: What is the best way to stop flu spreading? | Sneeze into your hands and shake them | Share cups and tissues with friends | Stay in bed and eat only sweets | *Cover coughs in a tissue or your elbow, and wash your hands
